!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section Cl2: Cl2 + hv --> Cl + Cl
! source : JPL-2006
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> "Halogens+mixed halogens" -> "Cl2" -> "JPL-2006"
! Rem1: Quantum yield = 1.
! Rem2: Temperature influence:
!       250-550nm: T dep. according to the formula:
!           crs = 1.e-20 * alpha**0.5 * (27.3 exp(-99*alpha * (ln(329.5/wl))**2) ...
!                   ... + 0.932 * exp(-91.5*alpha * (ln(406.5/wl))**2))
!       where alpha = tanh(402.7/T), and T the temperature.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
! Rem3: BE CAREFUL: The crs values provided below are not used for computing
!       the photodissociation constants since all the wl range is calculated
!       with the formula given above.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        80  | Finishes at wl interval :  142
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  no  from(nm) to(nm)  | crs (cm2) | qyield (0->1) |   
